1
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:54,971
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

2
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:59,142
The pneumatic tube system opening ceremony
is a major event

3
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:02,228
attended by high-ranking officials
like Gyeongseong's mayor,

4
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:04,814
the Central Advisory Council's vice chair,
foreign reporters,

5
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:06,941
and pro-Japanese businessmen
like Kim Seung-eok.

6
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:09,110
Among us, Philip and I will be attending.

7
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:11,738
Myung-nam, who is invited with her father,

8
00:01:11,821 --> 00:01:14,741
and Songjeon will also be there.

9
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:18,078
Songjeon, is it confirmed that
you'll be working as a kitchen assistant?

10
00:01:18,661 --> 00:01:23,333
Yes, since I'm Japanese, I passed
the background check without issue.

11
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:25,335
Thank you
for taking on this dangerous job.

12
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:27,170
I'm a member of the Gugukdan too.

13
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:29,255
On the day of the opening ceremony…

14
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:31,341
LADIES' ROOM

15
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:41,726
<i>I'll retrieve the three bombs</i>
<i>we've smuggled in</i>

16
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,520
<i>and assemble them into time bombs.</i>

17
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:55,949
<i>At 6:00 p.m.,</i>

18
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:59,119
<i>the ceremony will begin in the pneumatic</i>
<i>tube room on the first floor.</i>

19
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:03,748
<i>The governor-general, the inspector</i>
<i>general, Philip, and others will attend.</i>

20
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:12,549
<i>Meanwhile, Myung-nam and I</i>
<i>will wait with the other guests</i>

21
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:14,300
<i>in the second-floor banquet hall.</i>

22
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:15,844
Oh my, Ms. Myung-nam.

23
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:17,846
Hello.

24
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:33,111
<i>When the time comes…</i>

25
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:34,821
Fire!

26
00:02:34,904 --> 00:02:37,240
<i>Songjeon will set off the fire alarm</i>

27
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:40,034
<i>to distract the guests</i>
<i>in the banquet hall.</i>

28
00:02:45,123 --> 00:02:45,957
Yes, sir!

29
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:48,626
- Go see what's happening.
- Yes, sir!

30
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:53,089
Are you hurt?

31
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:54,883
What is going on?

32
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:56,134
I'm sorry.

33
00:02:56,217 --> 00:03:00,013
<i>I'll hide the bomb</i>
<i>in the floral arrangement on the stage.</i>

34
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:16,696
<i>It'll be right in front</i>
<i>of where the governor-general</i>

35
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:20,825
<i>and inspector general will stand</i>
<i>when they return after the ceremony.</i>

36
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:23,620
His Excellency the Governor-General
is arriving!

37
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:03,159
Raise your glasses!

38
00:04:12,001 --> 00:04:13,253
<i>As for the bomb,</i>

39
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:15,797
<i>when the governor-general</i>
<i>proposes a toast…</i>

40
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:19,717
Cheers!

41
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,219
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

42
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:23,096
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

43
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:30,687
<i>…it will go off.</i>

44
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:06,389
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

45
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:09,726
EPISODE 9

46
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:15,231
You're late.

47
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:34,917
What's this?

48
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:37,587
It's an identity guarantee letter.

49
00:05:39,922 --> 00:05:41,507
An identity guarantee letter?

50
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:44,719
You'll be leaving tomorrow night

51
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:46,471
for America.

52
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:48,348
Tomorrow?

53
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:49,307
That's right.

54
00:05:50,099 --> 00:05:53,561
The American missionary, Mr. Miller,
is returning to America with his family.

55
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:59,650
Mrs. Miller is taking a nanny to America
to care for her three-month-old baby.

56
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:01,444
The nanny's name is

57
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:03,404
Keum Seo-hee.

58
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:08,534
It's a document
where Mr. Miller guarantees your identity.

59
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:11,662
Philip went to a lot of trouble
to get it notarized at the U.S. Consulate.

60
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,915
Mr. Miller helped a great deal too.

61
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:22,006
There's one catch.
According to the document,

62
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:26,386
you'll have to leave America
within 30 days of entering the country.

63
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:31,474
Once you arrive in San Francisco
with the Miller family,

64
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:34,394
you'll be on your own.

65
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:36,979
You'll be staying illegally,

66
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:39,857
but it's the best we can do.
I hope you understand.

67
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:43,528
Sure.

68
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:45,780
Don't worry about me.

69
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:10,346
Don't worry about the banquet tomorrow.

70
00:07:10,972 --> 00:07:13,349
We've been cracking down
on independence fighters' hideouts

71
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,226
in Keijo since last week.

72
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:18,729
So far, we've arrested
six independence fighters

73
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:20,523
and 57 suspicious individuals.

74
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:23,568
Apologies for the interruption.

75
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:38,958
Allow me to pour you a drink.

76
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:40,126
Get out.

77
00:07:57,852 --> 00:07:59,812
They must've mistaken this
for another room.

78
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:02,273
I'll have a serious word with the owner.

79
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,985
They should know
you don't like having geisha around.

80
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:12,450
My apologies.

81
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:14,911
I spoke out of turn.

82
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:17,538
Any news on Keum Seok-jung's wife yet?

83
00:08:19,123 --> 00:08:21,876
We're still following leads
in the Kyeam-ri area.

84
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:24,587
We'll find out for certain
as soon as possible.

85
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:27,465
Find out how she's living if she's alive,

86
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:29,800
or how she died if she's dead.

87
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:33,721
Joseon women can be reckless.

88
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:37,225
We need to tie up all the loose ends.

89
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:40,520
Understood, sir!

90
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:45,816
Let me pour you another drink.

91
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:06,295
<i>You chose to become Japanese.</i>
<i>No one forced you.</i>

92
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:09,507
Remember who's given you
this life of luxury all this time.

93
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:11,884
However foolish you may be,

94
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:14,095
you should know you owe me some gratitude.

95
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:18,224
I really didn't steal anything.

96
00:09:18,307 --> 00:09:19,767
We were just looking.

97
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:21,811
What the hell are you yapping about?

98
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:26,190
Please let us go. We didn't do anything.

99
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:29,193
Hey! You got filthy water
all over my clothes.

100
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:30,945
You filthy little street rats!

101
00:09:31,028 --> 00:09:32,280
You stink!

102
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:34,282
Please, don't beat us.

103
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:36,284
You know what your problem is?

104
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:39,870
You live off Japan's generosity,

105
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:43,374
yet you never learn how to be grateful!

106
00:09:48,045 --> 00:09:49,046
Hey.

107
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,965
You there, gentleman.

108
00:09:51,048 --> 00:09:52,425
Just go on your way.

109
00:09:55,511 --> 00:09:56,554
Okay?

110
00:09:56,637 --> 00:10:00,308
I said, just be on your way.

111
00:10:04,061 --> 00:10:05,229
What the hell?

112
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:06,981
Don't you get what I'm saying?

113
00:10:09,066 --> 00:10:10,443
Are you <i>Josenjing?</i>

114
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:12,653
Right?

115
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:14,989
However well they clean up,

116
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:18,868
<i>Josenjings </i>still stink like animals--

117
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:29,420
Stop right there!

118
00:10:39,096 --> 00:10:39,972
Say that again.

119
00:10:41,015 --> 00:10:43,184
What did you say about <i>Josenjing?</i>

120
00:10:45,686 --> 00:10:46,520
Say that again.

121
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:48,773
Stop!

122
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:03,454
<i>Get out.</i>

123
00:11:05,706 --> 00:11:07,667
I said, get out of here, now!

124
00:11:10,127 --> 00:11:11,545
Did you find that amusing?

125
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:14,215
I said I didn't know

126
00:11:15,383 --> 00:11:17,426
whether to side with Joseon or Japan.

127
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:20,304
You think I deserve this?

128
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:23,265
Get out.

129
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:27,436
Get out of my sight right now!

130
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:35,861
He wanted me gone so badly.

131
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,533
Now I'm actually leaving.

132
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:45,162
Stop or I'll shoot you.

133
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:47,456
Put your hands up and turn around.

134
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:56,340
Go ahead.

135
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:58,634
What?

136
00:11:59,301 --> 00:12:00,177
You said you'd shoot.

137
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:01,679
What the hell are you saying?

138
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:04,557
I said, shoot me.
That's what you people do best.

139
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,809
Kill him, Officer Kimura!

140
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:10,354
What's your name?

141
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:14,066
I said, what's your name?

142
00:12:18,487 --> 00:12:20,531
I want you to contact me directly.

143
00:12:20,614 --> 00:12:22,533
The Government-General, not the residence.

144
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:26,704
Please forgive us!

145
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:29,290
Apologize to him now!

146
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:32,209
This gentleman is Mr. Sato Hideo,
son of the inspector general

147
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:33,919
of the Government-General.

148
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:35,629
- Forgive us!
- Forgive us!

149
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:38,340
We made a grave mistake.

150
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:40,384
Please forgive us!

151
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:41,844
Please forgive us!

152
00:12:45,014 --> 00:12:47,141
We have the utmost respect

153
00:12:47,224 --> 00:12:49,143
for Inspector General Sato Shinichi!

154
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:36,899
Welcome back.

155
00:13:36,982 --> 00:13:38,234
Welcome back.

156
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:54,083
By the way…

157
00:13:56,502 --> 00:13:57,628
What?

158
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:03,050
Hideo hasn't come home or sent word.

159
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:05,928
I'm worried his pneumothorax
might have returned.

160
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:07,680
There's no need to worry.

161
00:14:08,305 --> 00:14:09,139
Understood.

162
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,643
Have a good night.

163
00:14:32,162 --> 00:14:32,997
So-ran.

164
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:35,249
Yes?

165
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:41,839
Give me your hand for a second.

166
00:14:54,393 --> 00:14:57,605
I thought I'd get you something
for tomorrow's banquet.

167
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:59,315
I hope you like it.

168
00:15:00,816 --> 00:15:01,984
Thank you.

169
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,167
Don't worry about tomorrow's mission.

170
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:20,044
We'll pull it off for sure.

171
00:15:20,878 --> 00:15:23,255
We're going
to the Government-General tomorrow.

172
00:15:23,339 --> 00:15:24,965
There's no telling what might happen.

173
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:33,599
Do you remember what you said?

174
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:38,896
You said you'd take your own life
after killing Sato.

175
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:45,235
I wanted to ask you something.

176
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:49,865
"Is there really no place for me
in your world?"

177
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:59,416
You know how I feel about you, don't you?

178
00:16:01,585 --> 00:16:03,504
We may be posing as a married couple,

179
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:06,090
but my feelings for you
have always been real.

180
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:10,678
I'm sorry.

181
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:18,811
I understand.

182
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:32,700
But this mission is different
from the last one we carried out here.

183
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:35,619
This one's a time bomb.
You can make it out alive.

184
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:43,085
It's okay if you don't feel
the same way about me.

185
00:16:43,168 --> 00:16:45,713
Just don't even think about
killing yourself after this mission.

186
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:48,632
Philip.

187
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:51,593
- So-ran.
- I hope you understand.

188
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:56,390
After everything I've been through,

189
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:00,102
I think I'm a little exhausted.

190
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:09,528
Do you remember my request
to be cremated in <i>hanbok?</i>

191
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:13,741
I should've prepared it beforehand,
but I couldn't.

192
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:16,660
Please, I'm counting on you.

193
00:17:26,628 --> 00:17:30,591
We'll pull this off,
and you'll make it out alive.

194
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:33,927
If we fail, and that's a big if,

195
00:17:34,553 --> 00:17:36,305
I won't let you get hurt. Ever.

196
00:18:07,419 --> 00:18:08,253
Come in.

197
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:13,425
Hey.

198
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:17,012
Put your things in here
and take it with you.

199
00:18:20,265 --> 00:18:21,350
Thank you.

200
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:27,940
Go to Gyeongseong Station
right after the operation tomorrow.

201
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:32,111
Go straight to Incheon
and get on the morning boat.

202
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:34,279
I will.

203
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:36,323
Even if things don't go as planned,

204
00:18:37,282 --> 00:18:38,367
you'll still leave.

205
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:41,537
Because that was our deal.

206
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:47,876
Thank you for everything.

207
00:18:57,678 --> 00:19:00,931
What are you going to do
after the mission?

208
00:19:02,599 --> 00:19:03,475
I'm not sure.

209
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:06,812
I've never thought about it.

210
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:10,274
You can figure it out when it's over.

211
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:12,651
I suppose so.

212
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:16,738
All right, then. Sleep well.

213
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:19,408
You may not get much rest for a while,
starting tomorrow.

214
00:19:21,493 --> 00:19:22,578
Madam.

215
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:25,164
Yeah?

216
00:19:27,749 --> 00:19:28,584
Tomorrow…

217
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:32,629
everything will go just fine.

218
00:19:34,131 --> 00:19:34,965
I hope so.

219
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:37,843
Thanks.

220
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:12,419
You could become a suspect
after the operation tomorrow.

221
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:16,465
Do you think
I haven't prepared myself for that?

222
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:21,136
You kept sneaking out alone,

223
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:24,890
so I followed you
to see if you had a lover.

224
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:28,977
That eventually led me to the Gugukdan.

225
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:32,773
You see,

226
00:20:34,107 --> 00:20:37,027
I didn't join
the independence movement lightly.

227
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:40,530
I know.

228
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:49,331
Please don't get married, miss.

229
00:20:54,878 --> 00:20:56,505
Once tomorrow's operation is over,

230
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,549
leave for Shanghai.

231
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:04,721
With me.

232
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:18,610
- Songjeon.
- Hey.

233
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:22,281
Let's eat.

234
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:23,365
Here you go.

235
00:21:25,742 --> 00:21:26,576
Rice balls?

236
00:21:27,744 --> 00:21:29,413
- Did you make these?
- Yeah.

237
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,456
You said back in Yokohama,

238
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:33,709
your mother's rice balls
were your favorite.

239
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:38,171
This is all the rice I could get.

240
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:42,384
Come back safely tomorrow.

241
00:21:47,472 --> 00:21:48,307
Back then,

242
00:21:49,683 --> 00:21:50,892
when the earthquake hit…

243
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:54,855
I lost my whole family…

244
00:21:57,357 --> 00:22:00,652
and I nearly got killed
by the vigilante group.

245
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:05,407
You told them I was Japanese,
and that's what saved my life.

246
00:22:08,201 --> 00:22:09,619
I was truly

247
00:22:10,370 --> 00:22:11,621
grateful.

248
00:22:15,083 --> 00:22:16,335
I should be thanking you…

249
00:22:19,671 --> 00:22:20,547
for accepting me…

250
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:24,217
as your friend.

251
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:30,599
The rice will dry out.

252
00:22:30,682 --> 00:22:31,516
Eat up.

253
00:22:44,112 --> 00:22:44,988
That's so good.

254
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:47,491
But…

255
00:22:49,368 --> 00:22:50,327
you got any kimchi?

256
00:22:51,828 --> 00:22:53,121
Rice balls go best with kimchi.

257
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:54,331
Kimchi?

258
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:56,833
No, we're all out.

259
00:23:00,003 --> 00:23:00,921
Hey, Songjeon.

260
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:03,256
I mean, Mr. Matsuda.

261
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:06,551
What do you mean, kimchi?
Don't blow your cover.

262
00:23:12,891 --> 00:23:13,975
All right, let's eat.

263
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:58,019
Wipe them clean.
I don't want a single fingerprint!

264
00:24:00,689 --> 00:24:01,523
Hey!

265
00:24:02,065 --> 00:24:03,942
I told you not to leave fingerprints!

266
00:24:39,644 --> 00:24:40,645
Good morn…

267
00:24:46,651 --> 00:24:47,694
Good morning, sir.

268
00:24:51,072 --> 00:24:53,492
I hear the French technician
praised your English

269
00:24:54,075 --> 00:24:56,286
to the chief of Foreign Affairs.

270
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:01,291
You seem to get along well
with foreigners.

271
00:25:02,876 --> 00:25:03,919
That's kind of you to say.

272
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:07,297
Where'd you learn English?

273
00:25:08,381 --> 00:25:09,633
I picked it up as a child

274
00:25:10,592 --> 00:25:13,428
while working as a live-in maid
for foreigners.

275
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:17,349
I'd interpret for the lady of the house
when she went to the market.

276
00:25:24,064 --> 00:25:25,649
So that's why

277
00:25:26,274 --> 00:25:29,236
you interpreted so well
for that subversive before.

278
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:32,364
Yes.

279
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:33,657
His name was

280
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:36,159
Keum Seok-jung, wasn't it?

281
00:25:38,286 --> 00:25:40,830
I don't remember his name clearly.

282
00:25:41,581 --> 00:25:42,582
Oh, is that so?

283
00:25:43,750 --> 00:25:45,418
Isn't Keum rather a rare surname?

284
00:25:45,502 --> 00:25:47,921
I'm surprised you don't remember.

285
00:25:48,713 --> 00:25:50,840
I was too nervous while interpreting,

286
00:25:51,633 --> 00:25:53,635
so his name didn't stick.

287
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:56,763
He was nothing more
than a subversive, after all.

288
00:25:56,846 --> 00:25:58,974
You said it was easy
since you had so much experience.

289
00:26:00,141 --> 00:26:02,018
But you were too nervous
to remember his name?

290
00:26:04,354 --> 00:26:05,188
It's just--

291
00:26:08,441 --> 00:26:09,818
Of course you were nervous.

292
00:26:10,569 --> 00:26:12,737
Jongno Police Station
isn't just any local market.

293
00:26:14,864 --> 00:26:15,699
Indeed.

294
00:26:16,491 --> 00:26:18,618
You'll interpret for the foreign reporters

295
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:20,120
at today's opening ceremony.

296
00:26:22,789 --> 00:26:23,623
Me?

297
00:26:25,208 --> 00:26:27,127
What about Interpreter Sato?

298
00:26:27,210 --> 00:26:29,796
He's called in sick.
I hear a cold is going around.

299
00:26:31,881 --> 00:26:34,467
The pneumatic tube system opening ceremony
is an important event.

300
00:26:34,551 --> 00:26:35,552
I'm assigning it to you

301
00:26:35,635 --> 00:26:38,555
since we couldn't find an interpreter
for the technical terms right away.

302
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:41,474
Be sure not to make a single mistake.

303
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:44,269
Yes, sir.

304
00:26:44,352 --> 00:26:45,186
Very well.

305
00:26:51,568 --> 00:26:54,237
ENGLISH TRANSLATION UNIT

306
00:27:01,661 --> 00:27:04,080
INTERPRETER SATO HIDEO

307
00:27:11,463 --> 00:27:12,547
Hurry up!

308
00:27:43,453 --> 00:27:45,413
I don't get to see him before I leave.

309
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:01,513
I wanted to help him find his mother.

310
00:29:32,353 --> 00:29:33,730
You'll be leaving today, right?

311
00:29:33,813 --> 00:29:34,647
Yes.

312
00:29:35,815 --> 00:29:36,941
I'm so jealous.

313
00:29:37,650 --> 00:29:40,069
You can just turn your back on Joseon
and leave.

314
00:29:43,448 --> 00:29:45,617
I'm just as jealous of you.

315
00:29:47,118 --> 00:29:49,329
You have wealth, beauty,

316
00:29:49,412 --> 00:29:51,122
and someone good by your side.

317
00:29:51,873 --> 00:29:53,291
What? Someone good?

318
00:29:55,794 --> 00:29:58,296
I'm saying you're lucky
to have everything.

319
00:29:59,130 --> 00:29:59,964
If you'll excuse me.

320
00:30:08,681 --> 00:30:11,392
Who would've thought Keijo
would have a pneumatic tube system?

321
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:14,562
It fills me with pride
to see the Empire's greatness

322
00:30:14,646 --> 00:30:16,940
displayed to the world.

323
00:30:17,023 --> 00:30:20,568
The pneumatic tube system in Keijo isn't
just an administrative infrastructure.

324
00:30:20,652 --> 00:30:23,112
The banquet is quite splendid.

325
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:26,783
That's good to hear.

326
00:30:30,620 --> 00:30:31,746
Mr. Kim.

327
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:34,040
You're quite the businessman.

328
00:30:34,123 --> 00:30:37,919
I knew it when you made the enormous
donation to the pneumatic tube project.

329
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:40,338
And now you've become
the inspector general's in-law.

330
00:30:40,421 --> 00:30:41,965
There's no denying

331
00:30:42,048 --> 00:30:44,676
you're the star of tonight's banquet.

332
00:30:46,094 --> 00:30:47,303
Excuse me for a moment.

333
00:30:47,387 --> 00:30:48,221
Sure.

334
00:30:51,266 --> 00:30:52,183
Inspector general.

335
00:30:55,270 --> 00:30:57,939
Welcome, Mr. Yoo Philip.

336
00:30:58,523 --> 00:30:59,357
Mrs. Yoo.

337
00:30:59,941 --> 00:31:01,693
How have you been, Inspector General?

338
00:31:01,776 --> 00:31:03,778
It's an honor to be invited. Thank you.

339
00:31:03,862 --> 00:31:07,198
This event wouldn't mean as much
without you, Mr. Yoo.

340
00:31:09,158 --> 00:31:12,245
I'll write an excellent article
about the pneumatic tube opening ceremony.

341
00:31:12,328 --> 00:31:13,496
The whole world will see it

342
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:16,416
and be amazed to see
how developed Joseon has become.

343
00:31:18,167 --> 00:31:19,377
I'll look forward to it.

344
00:31:22,589 --> 00:31:25,800
I'm deeply sorry
about what happened to your baby.

345
00:31:29,512 --> 00:31:33,808
There's no greater pain for a parent
than losing a child.

346
00:31:43,359 --> 00:31:44,944
By the way, Inspector General,

347
00:31:45,028 --> 00:31:47,155
- about the opening ceremony--
- Yes.

348
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:49,782
Thank you

349
00:31:50,700 --> 00:31:51,701
for your kind words.

350
00:31:53,620 --> 00:31:55,496
I'm back, sir.

351
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:57,457
There you are.

352
00:31:58,958 --> 00:31:59,792
Hello, sir.

353
00:32:00,710 --> 00:32:01,586
We just arrived.

354
00:32:03,046 --> 00:32:04,839
During the opening ceremony,

355
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:07,717
Ms. Keum will interpret
for the foreign press.

356
00:32:10,094 --> 00:32:11,721
What a great honor.

357
00:32:11,804 --> 00:32:14,057
But Seo-hee's skills
are rather limited yet,

358
00:32:14,140 --> 00:32:15,600
so that worries me.

359
00:32:15,683 --> 00:32:18,269
I believe Mr. Hideo should do it instead.

360
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:19,187
Actually,

361
00:32:19,896 --> 00:32:23,066
Hideo called in sick with a cold today.

362
00:32:24,567 --> 00:32:26,194
Well, I suppose we have no choice, then.

363
00:32:28,655 --> 00:32:29,614
Inspector General.

364
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:32,492
If you'll excuse me.

365
00:32:32,575 --> 00:32:35,036
Yoon Deog-yeong
of the Central Advisory Council is here.

366
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:36,287
Sure.

367
00:32:41,834 --> 00:32:42,961
You have to interpret today?

368
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:47,840
Keum Seo-hee.

369
00:32:56,349 --> 00:32:57,892
Oh dear, what do I do?

370
00:32:57,976 --> 00:32:58,810
Where did it go?

371
00:32:58,893 --> 00:33:00,103
There it is.

372
00:33:02,271 --> 00:33:03,523
What's going on?

373
00:33:05,316 --> 00:33:08,319
Mrs. Yoo's button came off.

374
00:33:09,362 --> 00:33:10,989
There's a sewing kit in the office.

375
00:33:11,072 --> 00:33:12,949
May I take her to the office and help her?

376
00:33:13,032 --> 00:33:14,534
Then who's going to interpret?

377
00:33:15,535 --> 00:33:16,452
I'll do it.

378
00:33:22,542 --> 00:33:23,376
Go on, then.

379
00:33:24,377 --> 00:33:25,503
Thank you.

380
00:33:27,380 --> 00:33:28,381
Well then.

381
00:33:32,343 --> 00:33:33,970
Sorry about the commotion.

382
00:33:34,053 --> 00:33:35,430
It's quite all right.

383
00:33:37,390 --> 00:33:40,893
By the way, where is Hideo?

384
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:42,979
Hideo is--

385
00:33:43,062 --> 00:33:44,981
Good evening, everyone!

386
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:47,525
Hello, how are you all?

387
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:49,402
It's been a long time.

388
00:33:50,611 --> 00:33:52,363
Hello, it's good to see you again.

389
00:33:59,454 --> 00:34:00,830
Is that Hideo?

390
00:34:02,373 --> 00:34:03,624
Hello.

391
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:04,834
Good evening.

392
00:34:04,917 --> 00:34:06,127
Thanks.

393
00:34:06,919 --> 00:34:09,505
Good evening.

394
00:34:14,594 --> 00:34:18,723
Father, whom I respect above all others.

395
00:34:18,806 --> 00:34:21,309
There you are.

396
00:34:22,602 --> 00:34:26,397
I'm a little lat…

397
00:34:26,481 --> 00:34:28,149
No, wrong word. I meant "a little bit."

398
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:29,150
I'm a little bit late.

399
00:34:32,278 --> 00:34:34,864
I always thought Hideo was a goody-goody.

400
00:34:34,947 --> 00:34:37,200
It turns out he's quite the man.

401
00:34:38,076 --> 00:34:38,910
Yes, I am.

402
00:34:40,203 --> 00:34:41,913
Myung-nam, where have you been?

403
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:43,873
Why are you standing there?

404
00:34:43,956 --> 00:34:46,501
Why don't you come over
and say hi to Hideo?

405
00:34:49,378 --> 00:34:50,505
Good evening.

406
00:34:50,588 --> 00:34:51,881
There, there.

407
00:34:51,964 --> 00:34:54,926
You two make such a lovely couple.

408
00:34:55,009 --> 00:34:56,260
I couldn't agree more.

409
00:34:57,553 --> 00:34:59,472
How could we not make a lovely couple?

410
00:34:59,555 --> 00:35:01,516
My father, whom I deeply respect,

411
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:04,644
and Mr. Kim arranged this marriage.

412
00:35:04,727 --> 00:35:06,395
Exactly.

413
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:08,147
You two look wonderful together.

414
00:35:08,231 --> 00:35:10,483
Oh, to be young.

415
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:15,113
Yeah, all I have to do

416
00:35:15,196 --> 00:35:17,198
is do as I'm told.

417
00:35:18,407 --> 00:35:21,494
What should we name our baby?

418
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:22,954
If it's a girl,

419
00:35:23,538 --> 00:35:24,372
Haruko?

420
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:26,374
Akiko?

421
00:35:26,457 --> 00:35:27,583
"Ko" for "nose"?

422
00:35:28,167 --> 00:35:31,838
Well, Hideo, I think you've had
a bit much to drink.

423
00:35:32,588 --> 00:35:33,422
Father.

424
00:35:33,506 --> 00:35:36,342
I'm doing well, aren't I?

425
00:35:36,425 --> 00:35:38,386
I'm doing everything you told me to do!

426
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:40,972
Isn't that right?

427
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:52,275
You're still going strong.

428
00:35:52,942 --> 00:35:55,069
What kind of behavior is this, Sato Hideo?

429
00:35:56,696 --> 00:35:58,322
"Sato Hideo."

430
00:35:58,406 --> 00:35:59,365
What?

431
00:36:00,283 --> 00:36:02,076
You don't have to remind me.

432
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:06,956
I know my own name perfectly well.

433
00:36:19,552 --> 00:36:20,720
Take it to the banquet.

434
00:36:21,512 --> 00:36:23,181
You never know what might happen.

435
00:36:23,764 --> 00:36:27,852
We'll discuss the consequences
of your behavior after the banquet.

436
00:37:05,765 --> 00:37:09,936
I heard there was quite a spectacle
at the banquet, so I was on my way there.

437
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:14,315
And here I've run
into the star of the show.

438
00:37:16,609 --> 00:37:19,946
I made sure
there'd be no disturbance outside.

439
00:37:21,447 --> 00:37:24,033
Little did I know
the real trouble would be in here.

440
00:37:26,702 --> 00:37:28,537
So much for

441
00:37:29,163 --> 00:37:30,957
all that effort.

442
00:37:31,958 --> 00:37:33,084
Hideo.

443
00:37:33,167 --> 00:37:35,253
You should show proper respect

444
00:37:35,878 --> 00:37:37,713
when addressing your superior's son.

445
00:37:38,297 --> 00:37:41,342
Don't call me Hideo.
It's Mr. Sato, you little shit.

446
00:37:44,929 --> 00:37:48,057
You and I are both Japan's dogs.

447
00:37:48,766 --> 00:37:50,893
Let's not bite each other.

448
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:15,584
You're wearing earrings today.

449
00:38:19,922 --> 00:38:22,174
They don't seem like your style.

450
00:38:23,467 --> 00:38:24,719
Someone bought them for you?

451
00:38:27,096 --> 00:38:29,473
Was it Mr. Yoo?

452
00:38:35,062 --> 00:38:36,314
I got one done.

453
00:38:38,190 --> 00:38:39,108
Okay.

454
00:38:43,779 --> 00:38:45,156
They look good on you.

455
00:38:46,157 --> 00:38:46,991
They're pretty.

456
00:38:48,200 --> 00:38:50,870
So, why didn't Sato Hideo
come to work today?

457
00:38:53,247 --> 00:38:54,540
I have no idea.

458
00:38:54,623 --> 00:38:56,751
But it's probably for the best.

459
00:38:56,834 --> 00:38:58,711
You can assemble them here.

460
00:38:58,794 --> 00:39:01,756
This is better than the restroom.

461
00:39:09,513 --> 00:39:10,723
Who is it?

462
00:39:16,312 --> 00:39:17,813
Who is it?

463
00:39:17,897 --> 00:39:18,814
It's me.

464
00:39:20,441 --> 00:39:21,359
Open the door.

465
00:39:21,901 --> 00:39:23,069
Why's the door locked?

466
00:39:23,652 --> 00:39:24,945
Yes, Interpreter Sato.

467
00:39:27,865 --> 00:39:30,409
Mrs. Yoo's button fell off.

468
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:32,703
I'm sewing it back on for her.
Just a moment.

469
00:39:32,787 --> 00:39:33,621
Wait. Just one more.

470
00:39:33,704 --> 00:39:35,373
- It'll be quick.
- No, he's right outside.

471
00:39:36,374 --> 00:39:37,583
Who could be in there?

472
00:39:38,959 --> 00:39:39,877
Dad.

473
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:41,587
We can look around another time.

474
00:39:41,670 --> 00:39:43,172
Nonsense, why wait?

475
00:39:43,255 --> 00:39:46,133
I just want to have a look
at my son-in-law's office.

476
00:39:46,217 --> 00:39:48,094
Surely you can't make me
turn back at the door.

477
00:39:48,177 --> 00:39:49,720
Don't you agree?

478
00:39:51,013 --> 00:39:52,056
That's right.

479
00:40:01,107 --> 00:40:03,025
Who's inside? Why the wait?

480
00:40:03,651 --> 00:40:04,985
Please bear with us for a moment.

481
00:40:06,153 --> 00:40:07,154
Come on, Dad.

482
00:40:18,999 --> 00:40:19,834
Mr. Sato.

483
00:40:20,751 --> 00:40:22,336
You're here.

484
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:23,796
Let's go in.

485
00:40:25,798 --> 00:40:28,509
And at last, here we are!

486
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:32,638
This is my son-in-law's office.

487
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:40,855
You know how well
my son-in-law speaks English?

488
00:40:41,397 --> 00:40:44,400
If Hideo succeeds me,

489
00:40:44,483 --> 00:40:48,654
Joil Textile Factory
will be more successful than ever!

490
00:40:50,406 --> 00:40:52,491
You must feel very reassured.

491
00:40:53,159 --> 00:40:54,452
I'm really envious.

492
00:40:54,535 --> 00:40:55,661
I'll do my best.

493
00:40:55,744 --> 00:40:56,912
I'd appreciate your guidance.

494
00:40:59,081 --> 00:41:00,749
By the way, who is this lady?

495
00:41:01,667 --> 00:41:02,668
This is--

496
00:41:02,751 --> 00:41:06,213
She's the wife of Yoo Philip,
an American correspondent from WWP News.

497
00:41:07,214 --> 00:41:09,467
An American reporter's wife?

498
00:41:10,426 --> 00:41:11,760
What was she doing here?

499
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:14,472
I was helping her repair a button
on her clothes.

500
00:41:15,055 --> 00:41:16,515
It's done now, you may leave.

501
00:41:22,563 --> 00:41:23,397
Wait.

502
00:41:24,273 --> 00:41:26,108
Why isn't that maid going with her?

503
00:41:26,192 --> 00:41:28,569
- This is--
- Sorry for the late introduction.

504
00:41:28,652 --> 00:41:31,739
I'm working alongside Mr. Sato
as an interpreter trainee.

505
00:41:32,656 --> 00:41:34,325
A female interpreter?

506
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:38,537
Well, if Hideo is training you,
I suppose there's little to worry.

507
00:41:39,121 --> 00:41:42,166
Even so, isn't it a bit inappropriate
for a man and a woman

508
00:41:42,249 --> 00:41:43,709
to share an office every day?

509
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:47,546
In any case,

510
00:41:47,630 --> 00:41:50,716
look at Myung-nam and Hideo.

511
00:41:50,799 --> 00:41:53,385
They're a picture-perfect pair,
aren't they?

512
00:41:53,469 --> 00:41:54,303
Absolutely.

513
00:41:56,639 --> 00:41:59,975
Myung-nam, stand a little closer to Hideo.

514
00:42:02,478 --> 00:42:06,190
She's never been around any men
except for me,

515
00:42:06,273 --> 00:42:08,317
so she's terribly shy.

516
00:42:10,569 --> 00:42:11,403
Right.

517
00:42:11,487 --> 00:42:13,656
Why don't you link arms
like you did before?

518
00:42:13,739 --> 00:42:15,407
Like a happy couple.

519
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:19,078
Here, take my arm.

520
00:42:23,415 --> 00:42:25,626
There we go!

521
00:42:25,709 --> 00:42:28,087
A man ought to know how to take charge.

522
00:42:29,630 --> 00:42:32,341
He's charismatic and lacks for nothing.

523
00:42:32,424 --> 00:42:34,718
Absolutely.
I'll make sure Myung-nam learns

524
00:42:34,802 --> 00:42:37,638
how to make a good hangover soup
before they get married.

525
00:42:37,721 --> 00:42:38,556
Already?

526
00:42:39,974 --> 00:42:40,933
Myung-nam.

527
00:42:41,016 --> 00:42:44,186
You should come with us
to the pneumatic tube opening ceremony.

528
00:42:45,688 --> 00:42:46,564
Me?

529
00:42:50,651 --> 00:42:53,904
You told me to wait in the banquet hall
because that place is cramped.

530
00:42:53,988 --> 00:42:56,740
You should see
this marvelous new technology

531
00:42:56,824 --> 00:42:58,242
that I'm funding, right?

532
00:42:58,826 --> 00:43:01,412
So I asked your father-in-law
for a special favor.

533
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:05,124
It must be nice to call him your in-law.

534
00:43:06,041 --> 00:43:07,167
He's right.

535
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:10,087
Your father spent a whopping 100,000 won
on the project.

536
00:43:10,170 --> 00:43:11,755
You should see it for yourself.

537
00:43:11,839 --> 00:43:14,091
I get uncomfortable in tight spaces.

538
00:43:14,174 --> 00:43:15,384
I'll stay in the banquet hall.

539
00:43:15,467 --> 00:43:16,510
Why's that?

540
00:43:16,594 --> 00:43:18,512
Do you have something to do there?

541
00:43:23,392 --> 00:43:24,268
Not really.

542
00:43:25,227 --> 00:43:26,395
Okay. I'll go with you.

543
00:43:26,478 --> 00:43:27,479
Very well.

544
00:43:27,563 --> 00:43:30,024
Your father-in-law is being so thoughtful.

545
00:43:30,107 --> 00:43:31,483
You should certainly come.

546
00:43:33,277 --> 00:43:34,361
You can go on ahead.

547
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:35,946
I'll get changed and join you.

548
00:43:36,030 --> 00:43:37,948
Sure. Take your time.

549
00:43:38,032 --> 00:43:39,241
Now, let's head down.

550
00:43:39,325 --> 00:43:40,159
Let's go.

551
00:43:55,174 --> 00:43:57,509
I heard you weren't coming today.

552
00:43:59,511 --> 00:44:00,387
But here you are.

553
00:44:02,848 --> 00:44:04,016
Mr. Sato.

554
00:44:05,059 --> 00:44:06,018
Your lips…

555
00:44:11,273 --> 00:44:13,734
Have you been drinking?

556
00:44:15,069 --> 00:44:16,695
That's none of your business.

557
00:44:20,532 --> 00:44:21,367
What?

558
00:44:23,369 --> 00:44:25,329
Do you want to call me a pathetic loser

559
00:44:26,121 --> 00:44:28,582
who gets drunk
and goes around picking fights

560
00:44:29,541 --> 00:44:30,876
because my father chewed me out?

561
00:44:32,461 --> 00:44:33,295
Mr. Sato.

562
00:44:33,379 --> 00:44:35,673
Do you think you've got me
all figured out?

563
00:44:35,756 --> 00:44:38,634
So you think you can stick your nose
into my business?

564
00:44:50,020 --> 00:44:50,979
I'm sorry.

565
00:44:52,147 --> 00:44:54,608
I had no right to pry.

566
00:44:57,403 --> 00:44:59,321
I'll head downstairs.

567
00:44:59,905 --> 00:45:00,989
I'll leave you alone.

568
00:45:10,708 --> 00:45:11,542
Hold on.

569
00:45:13,585 --> 00:45:14,712
What's this here?

570
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:27,224
Sorry?

571
00:45:27,307 --> 00:45:28,517
This.

572
00:45:29,393 --> 00:45:30,519
This pawn ticket.

573
00:45:32,146 --> 00:45:33,564
Why'd you put it here?

574
00:45:36,024 --> 00:45:37,484
Why give it back out of the blue?

575
00:45:37,985 --> 00:45:39,820
Are you going somewhere? Or…

576
00:45:44,366 --> 00:45:45,909
do you not want anything to do

577
00:45:47,536 --> 00:45:49,371
with someone like me anymore?

578
00:45:55,461 --> 00:45:58,130
I think it's time I gave this back to you.

579
00:46:01,091 --> 00:46:04,261
You have your own path, and I have mine.

580
00:46:04,344 --> 00:46:05,929
We each have our own way to go.

581
00:46:09,475 --> 00:46:14,313
I know I've overstepped my bounds.
Thank you for putting up with me.

582
00:46:15,647 --> 00:46:16,899
Thank you for everything.

583
00:46:31,955 --> 00:46:33,457
I liked you.

584
00:46:38,253 --> 00:46:41,548
<i>Though I'd never see you again</i>
<i>after tomorrow.</i>

585
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:43,801
I liked

586
00:46:45,469 --> 00:46:48,430
for who you were as Kim Tae-ung.

587
00:46:57,940 --> 00:47:00,526
I guess that's why
I couldn't help getting involved.

588
00:47:12,204 --> 00:47:13,038
My name is…

589
00:47:14,665 --> 00:47:15,958
Sato Hideo.

590
00:47:20,754 --> 00:47:22,005
I'm not Kim Tae-ung.

591
00:48:01,837 --> 00:48:03,589
<i>The opening ceremony will wrap up…</i>

592
00:48:05,716 --> 00:48:08,176
<i>with the governor-general</i>
<i>receiving a congratulatory message</i>

593
00:48:08,260 --> 00:48:11,597
<i>from the Japanese Prime Minister via</i>
<i>pneumatic tube from the Keijo Post Office.</i>

594
00:48:13,765 --> 00:48:16,727
The very first item to arrive
through the pneumatic tube

595
00:48:16,810 --> 00:48:19,646
that launched in Keijo today…

596
00:48:23,859 --> 00:48:28,155
The celebratory letter
from Prime Minister Inukai!

597
00:48:33,452 --> 00:48:37,706
This just came from the Keijo Post Office!

598
00:48:43,337 --> 00:48:46,757
<i>Then Ga-kyung will signal Songjeon.</i>

599
00:48:46,840 --> 00:48:48,550
Please put me through to the kitchen.

600
00:48:49,259 --> 00:48:50,469
Yes, certainly.

601
00:48:50,552 --> 00:48:52,638
They must be parched.

602
00:48:53,680 --> 00:48:55,641
Understood. Thank you.

603
00:48:57,434 --> 00:49:00,771
His Excellency the Governor-General will
head to the banquet hall in five minutes!

604
00:49:00,854 --> 00:49:01,980
- Yes, chef!
- Yes, chef!

605
00:49:07,778 --> 00:49:09,029
Fire!

606
00:49:10,739 --> 00:49:11,865
Someone get water!

607
00:49:26,588 --> 00:49:27,798
What's going on?

608
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:34,638
Yes, sir.

609
00:49:45,774 --> 00:49:46,942
Go see what's going on.

610
00:49:47,025 --> 00:49:47,859
Yes, sir.

611
00:49:49,736 --> 00:49:50,612
Is everything okay?

612
00:49:52,197 --> 00:49:54,825
Please remain calm, everyone!

613
00:49:56,368 --> 00:49:57,619
We're looking into it.

614
00:49:57,703 --> 00:49:58,787
Please wait a moment!

615
00:49:58,870 --> 00:50:00,622
Tell us what's going on!

616
00:50:13,301 --> 00:50:14,636
<i>The bomb will explode</i>

617
00:50:14,720 --> 00:50:17,639
<i>during the governor-general's toast</i>
<i>at the banquet.</i>

618
00:50:17,723 --> 00:50:20,517
There are very important people upstairs.

619
00:50:21,101 --> 00:50:23,478
What were you thinking,
setting off the alarm, you idiot?

620
00:50:23,562 --> 00:50:24,479
I'm sorry.

621
00:50:26,356 --> 00:50:27,232
What's going on?

622
00:50:28,567 --> 00:50:29,735
Nothing to worry about.

623
00:50:29,818 --> 00:50:31,945
Someone set off the fire alarm by mistake.

624
00:50:32,529 --> 00:50:34,406
Seriously, be more careful!

625
00:50:34,489 --> 00:50:35,323
Yes, sir.

626
00:50:38,076 --> 00:50:39,202
Everything's fine.

627
00:50:40,328 --> 00:50:41,538
Don't be concerned.

628
00:50:41,621 --> 00:50:42,873
There's no problem.

629
00:50:45,167 --> 00:50:46,168
Let's carry on.

630
00:50:54,634 --> 00:50:55,802
It was a false alarm.

631
00:50:56,386 --> 00:50:58,472
Everyone, there's no need to worry.

632
00:50:59,222 --> 00:51:01,349
The fire alarm was triggered by mistake.

633
00:51:04,770 --> 00:51:07,105
Please enjoy the rest of the evening.

634
00:51:09,775 --> 00:51:11,651
I heard you're from Shanghai.

635
00:51:14,738 --> 00:51:18,033
I used to live in Shanghai.

636
00:51:19,785 --> 00:51:20,994
I'm sorry.

637
00:51:21,078 --> 00:51:24,206
I don't speak Japanese well.

638
00:51:25,874 --> 00:51:29,044
I speak a little Chinese.

639
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:35,425
Where in Shanghai did you live?

640
00:51:38,261 --> 00:51:39,721
- I--
- Oh my.

641
00:51:41,056 --> 00:51:42,182
One moment.

642
00:51:48,188 --> 00:51:49,689
What's the matter, ma'am?

643
00:52:03,829 --> 00:52:04,746
Maruyama.

644
00:52:05,330 --> 00:52:06,164
Yes, ma'am.

645
00:52:06,248 --> 00:52:08,125
Get these flowers out of here now.

646
00:52:11,169 --> 00:52:14,464
The governor-general
gets hay fever from roses!

647
00:52:15,257 --> 00:52:17,676
What kind of secretary doesn't know that?

648
00:52:17,759 --> 00:52:19,803
He'll be here shortly.

649
00:52:19,886 --> 00:52:21,138
Get them out of here now!

650
00:52:21,221 --> 00:52:23,181
Right away! I'm so sorry!

651
00:52:30,981 --> 00:52:32,607
Sorry about that.

652
00:52:34,192 --> 00:52:38,530
Where in Shanghai did you live?

653
00:52:42,909 --> 00:52:45,036
Well then, let's head to the banquet hall.

654
00:53:13,106 --> 00:53:13,940
What?

655
00:53:31,416 --> 00:53:33,501
Darn it, why are these out here?

656
00:53:47,682 --> 00:53:48,892
What do I do with it?

657
00:53:59,486 --> 00:54:00,320
Watch out.

658
00:54:05,158 --> 00:54:06,284
You must be busy.

659
00:54:06,368 --> 00:54:07,786
Can I give you a hand?

660
00:54:07,869 --> 00:54:09,329
No, thanks.

661
00:54:12,457 --> 00:54:14,042
This cake is really…

662
00:54:15,752 --> 00:54:17,295
enormous.

663
00:54:17,379 --> 00:54:19,714
I've never seen a cake this big
in my life.

664
00:54:19,798 --> 00:54:22,050
We got held up because of the fire alarm.

665
00:54:22,133 --> 00:54:24,094
Has the governor-general arrived yet?

666
00:54:24,177 --> 00:54:25,470
Not yet.

667
00:54:25,553 --> 00:54:26,596
That's a relief.

668
00:54:40,026 --> 00:54:41,945
The gift is in the cake.

669
00:55:11,558 --> 00:55:13,977
It'll go off at 6:20 p.m.
Get as far away as you can.

670
00:55:20,066 --> 00:55:21,109
It's in the cake.

671
00:55:50,597 --> 00:55:53,850
His Excellency is here!

672
00:56:26,383 --> 00:56:30,887
Today, May 15th, 1932,

673
00:56:31,471 --> 00:56:33,473
Joseon's first pneumatic tube system

674
00:56:33,556 --> 00:56:36,267
has successfully been unveiled!

675
00:56:42,732 --> 00:56:47,112
The Great Japanese Empire's efforts
for the development of Joseon

676
00:56:47,195 --> 00:56:51,449
have finally borne fruit today.

677
00:56:52,492 --> 00:56:53,451
This marks

678
00:56:54,160 --> 00:56:58,456
a new milestone in Joseon's modernization

679
00:56:58,998 --> 00:57:02,794
and the first step
toward Manseon's prosperity…

680
00:57:04,129 --> 00:57:05,213
MANSEON
MANCHURIA AND JOSEON

681
00:57:05,296 --> 00:57:07,632
…eventually reaching Manchukuo!

682
00:57:31,781 --> 00:57:33,450
Interpreter Sato!

683
00:57:34,993 --> 00:57:36,661
Interpreter Sato, over here.

684
00:57:46,171 --> 00:57:48,882
Interpret my speech into English.

685
00:57:50,008 --> 00:57:51,009
Yes, sir.

686
00:58:42,143 --> 00:58:43,019
Interpreter Sato.

687
00:58:45,772 --> 00:58:48,149
Why don't you join us for a toast?

688
00:58:52,987 --> 00:58:53,821
Yes, sir.

689
00:59:09,003 --> 00:59:10,255
Raise your glasses.

690
00:59:19,889 --> 00:59:22,392
<i>It'll go off at 6:20 p.m.</i>
<i>Get as far away as you can.</i>

691
00:59:25,895 --> 00:59:27,146
Cheers!

692
00:59:28,064 --> 00:59:29,274
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

693
01:00:19,032 --> 01:00:22,952
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

694
01:00:26,748 --> 01:00:29,125
<i>There's no shortage of people</i>
<i>who want me dead.</i>

695
01:00:29,208 --> 01:00:31,085
Mr. Sato!

696
01:00:33,171 --> 01:00:35,173
We'll all get caught if we don't hurry.

697
01:00:35,256 --> 01:00:36,549
<i>You should go already.</i>

698
01:00:36,633 --> 01:00:37,884
<i>I'm done going easy on you.</i>

699
01:00:37,967 --> 01:00:38,801
Kill him.

700
01:00:40,553 --> 01:00:41,596
<i>Don't forget.</i>

701
01:00:41,679 --> 01:00:43,931
You're nobody if I'm dead.

702
01:00:44,015 --> 01:00:46,309
I'll make sure
we catch the culprit tonight.

703
01:00:47,310 --> 01:00:48,394
<i>Ga-kyung.</i>

704
01:00:49,354 --> 01:00:50,647
<i>Be happy.</i>

705
01:00:58,029 --> 01:01:00,031
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
